{{!--
  Custom Handlebars template for the .desktop entry (bundle.linux.deb.desktopTemplate).
  Handlebars comments are stripped, so none of this reaches the installed file.

  It exists for one line: `Exec={{exec}} %F`. The bundler's built-in template emits
  a bare `Exec=gera`, so "Open with gera" from a file manager launched an empty
  window -- the MimeType line registered gera as a handler, but the path was never
  passed (verified on the 0.1.0 deb, 2026-09-07). %F hands over the local file(s).

  MimeType is hardcoded here because the template only receives `categories`,
  `comment`, `exec`, `icon` and `name` -- the fileAssociations entry in
  tauri.conf.json does not reach it. Keep the two in sync.
--}}
[Desktop Entry]
Categories={{categories}}
{{#if comment}}
Comment={{comment}}
{{/if}}
Exec={{exec}} %F
StartupWMClass={{exec}}
Icon={{icon}}
Name={{name}}
Terminal=false
Type=Application
MimeType=text/markdown;
